From 0d8c5f8ddd55de8a9120895e4d8d58bdbe9281e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xtu <xtu@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] feat(DSv4.1): decoder-side SWA bounded replay for
 DeepSeek-V4.1

Layers past the last KV source layer own only sliding-window KV, so during prefill they need only each
request's trailing window. The layer loop is factored into _run_layers and _collapse so the replay layers can
run on a subset of rows, and _decoder_replay_supported declines with a warning when the pipeline stage or the
parallelism setup cannot follow the smaller batch. Ported by hand from the CED branch following its diff, with
our SM80 fuse_mhc_all_reduce behaviour preserved inside _collapse.
